    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "using a Bland-Altman 10 plot of all samples with values in both assays (35 samples). The overall bias between the laboratorydeveloped assay and ASR was calculated from this plot using GraphPad Prism 5 Software (GraphPad Software, San Diego, CA). In addition, using proficiency samples provided by the American Society of Transplantation (AST, Mt Laurel, NJ) and Quality Control for Molecular Diagnostics (QCMD, Glasgow, Scotland), we determined results obtained from both assays."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 83,
    "level" : "Doctitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 41.667, 565.667, 82.333, 577.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "UniversLTStd-Bold",
    "font size" : 11.0,
    "text color" : "[0.669998, 0.0, 0.029998999999999998]",
    "content" : "Results"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 86,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 40.333, 534.0, 205.0, 547.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Limits of Detection and Quantification"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 87,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 40.333, 440.667, 286.333, 533.667 ],
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The LOD of the ASR was 2.25 log 10 copies/mL (180 copies/mL) ❚ Table 1 ❚ , which was equivalent to 1.30 log 10 copies/mL (20 copies/mL) using the Namalwa cell line. The LOQ based on an SD of 0.15 log 10 copies/mL or less was 3.90 log 10   copies/mL (Table 1). Of note, the SDs at 3.53 log 10 copies/mL and 2.89 log 10 copies/mL were 0.18 and 0.17 log 10 copies/mL, respectively."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 89,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 40.0, 416.667, 169.667, 430.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Linearity and Reproducibility"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 91,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 40.333, 285.0, 286.333, 415.667 ],
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The assay was linear from 2.17 to 6.21 log 10 copies/mL ❚ Figure 1 ❚ , with an R 2 value of 0.9925 (y = 1.0119x – 0.1184). Reproducibility was assessed by testing 7 replicates of low and high viral load patient samples and 6 replicates of the QSs. The low patient sample had a mean (SD, CV) value of 3.70 log 10 copies/mL (0.07, 2.0%). The high patient sample had a mean (SD, CV) value of 5.40 log 10 copies/mL (0.07, 1.4%). The QSs had mean Ct (SD, CV) values as follows: QS1, 21.8 (0.4, 1.6%); QS2, 25.1 (0.4, 1.5%); QS3, 28.5 (0.2, 0.8%); and QS4, 31.8 (0.3, 1.0%)."
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 82,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 302.124, 572.119, 537.801, 728.297 ],
