    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 383.333, 570.333, 487.0, 582.667 ],
    "font" : "Helvetica-Bold",
    "font size" : 7.92,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "log 10 Cell Line (copies/mL)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 85,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 299.333, 473.0, 534.333, 562.333 ],
    "font" : "UniversLTStd-Light",
    "font size" : 9.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "❚ Figure 1 ❚ Linearity plot. The mean values for each concentration from 2.44 to 6.21 log 10 copies/mL were plotted, with error bars representing the SD. A linear regression line (y = 1.0119x – 0.1184) was plotted with Microsoft Excel 2003 software (Redmond, WA), with an R 2   value of 0.9925, indicating that the assay is linear at least across this range."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 88,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 301.0, 430.0, 350.333, 442.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Agreement"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 90,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 299.667, 298.0, 545.333, 430.0 ],
    "font" : "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Of the 61 patient samples tested by the laboratorydeveloped method and the ASR, 35 were positive in both assays. Of the 6 samples that were positive in the Artus assay but not in the laboratory-developed assay, the average copy number was 1.62 log 10 copies/mL, with a range of 1.41 to 2.13 log 10 copies/mL. There was only 1 sample that was positive in the laboratory-developed assay but negative in the Artus assay, with a value of 3.23 log 10 copies/mL. The remaining 19 samples were negative by both assays. The 35 samples that were positive in both assays were plotted in a standard 10"
  }, {
